/* ============================================================
 * IMPULSE VAULT — lib/three.min.js  (PLACEHOLDER — REPLACE ME)
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * This is NOT the real Three.js. It is an empty placeholder so the
 * extension loads without error. The dashboard's 3D vault scene will
 * automatically fall back to a CSS visual until you drop the real
 * file here.
 *
 * >>> TO ENABLE THE 3D SCENE <<<
 *   1. Download the minified UMD build of Three.js (r150+ works well
 *      with this code, which uses MeshPhysicalMaterial transmission):
 *        https://unpkg.com/three@0.160.0/build/three.min.js
 *      (or grab build/three.min.js from https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js)
 *   2. Save it OVER this file at: impulse-vault/lib/three.min.js
 *   3. Reload the extension at chrome://extensions.
 *
 * Why local and not a CDN? Manifest V3's Content Security Policy
 * blocks remote scripts in extension pages, so Three.js must be
 * bundled as a local file. We never load anything from the network.
 *
 * This placeholder intentionally defines nothing, so `typeof THREE`
 * stays "undefined" and dashboard/vault3d.js renders the fallback.
 * ============================================================ */
